WEBVTT

english-sentence-completeness-narration-caption-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.435
Show me: first locate who or what the words are about. In ‘The curious fox waited,’ the subject is ‘the curious fox.’

english-sentence-completeness-narration-caption-2
00:00:06.435 --> 00:00:14.410
Talk me through it: find the subject, find what that subject does or is, ask whether the thought stands alone, and only then choose the end mark.

english-sentence-completeness-narration-caption-3
00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.755
Let’s do one together. Which predicate completes the subject ‘The small robot’?

english-sentence-completeness-narration-caption-4
00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:27.170
Different example: ‘When the rain stopped’ has a subject and verb, but when leaves us waiting. Add your own independent thought, then choose punctuation.
